+# 👥 Team server
+
+🌐 **English** · [Français](Team-Server.fr)
+
+A WorkPilot server shares a team's projects: one board everyone sees live, runs that execute on
+the server (each one sees only its own project), isolated organisations, roles, groups, quotas and
+an audit log. The desktop app, the phone app and AI apps (over MCP) connect to it.
+
+> The full guide, with every format and example (in French):
+> [docs/server-guide.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/server-guide.md).
+> Operations (TLS, backups, upgrades, logs):
+> [docs/server-operations.md](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/server-operations.md).
+
+## Where to host it
+
+Each team picks; the code is the same:
+
+| Choice | For | Address in the app |
+|---|---|---|
+| `public` | a VPS or a server with a DNS name, a distributed team | `https://<name>` (automatic Let's Encrypt certificate) |
+| `lan` | a machine on the local network (a company server, a member's PC) | `http://<IP or machine name>` |
+| `local` | this computer only, to try it | `http://localhost` |
+
+## Quick start
+
+On the host (Linux with Docker 23+, or Docker Desktop on Windows for `lan` and `local`):
+
+```bash
+cd deploy
+python3 configure.py --hosting lan --host 192.168.1.20   # or public / local
+# add the LLM provider's credentials to .env.server, for example
+# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=...
+docker compose --env-file .env.server up -d --build
+docker compose --env-file .env.server exec api \
+  python -m server.scripts.create_admin admin@example.com --name "First Last"
+```
+
+`configure.py` writes `.env.server` (secrets generated once, never replaced afterwards), the
+`Caddyfile` and the proxy override. Then, in the desktop app: the server's address, then the
+account you created.
+
+## The `.env.server` file
+
+One variable per line, `NAME=value`, no quotes; `#` for a comment. Excerpt:
+
+```bash
+WORKPILOT_HOSTING=public
+WORKPILOT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://workpilot.example.com
+WORKPILOT_PUBLIC_STREAM_URL=wss://workpilot.example.com
+CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=<token>
+OPENAI_API_KEY=<key>
+WORKPILOT_ENTRA_TENANT_ID=<tenant>          # Microsoft sign-in, optional
+WORKPILOT_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com        # invitation email, optional
+WORKPILOT_MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=6
+WORKPILOT_APPROVAL_QUORUM=low=1,medium=1,high=2
+```
+
+Never commit it, and keep a copy off the server: it holds the key that encrypts everyone's tokens.
+
+## Configure the team
+
+In the desktop app, **Administration** menu:
+
+- **Organizations**: one sealed space per team or client;
+- **Invitations**: a single-use link, emailed or handed over, with the role;
+- **Members**, **Roles & permissions**: eight built-in roles (Owner, Administrator, Maintainer,
+  Contributor by default, Reviewer, Operator, Analyst, Viewer) and your own;
+- **Groups**: a role and projects given to several people at once;
+- **Quotas**: members, projects, concurrent runs, monthly token budget;
+- **Audit**: who did what, exported as JSON.
+
+A project is a git repository the server clones with its own SSH key
+(`git@github.com:team/app.git`, or `https://…` without credentials in the URL).
+
+## Use it
+
+- **Desktop app**: sign-in screen at first launch (password, Microsoft, SSO or "I have an
+  invitation"); from local mode, **Settings → Team server**. Your GitHub, GitLab, Jira… tokens for
+  your runs: **Settings → My tokens on the server**.
+- **Phone**: the same address; over `http://`, only a private IP, a machine name without a dot or
+  ending in `.local`.
+- **AI apps**: **Settings → Integrations → MCP access to the server** makes a `wpat_…` token, then
+  for example
+  `claude mcp add --transport http workpilot https://workpilot.example.com/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer wpat_…"`.
+- **API**: `POST /auth/login`, then `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`; projects, cards, runs
+  and administration with `curl` in the guide.
+
+## Quick troubleshooting
+
+| Symptom | What to do |
+|---|---|
+| `docker compose` asks for `POSTGRES_PASSWORD` | add `--env-file .env.server` to every command |
+| The board does not update live | set `WORKPILOT_PUBLIC_STREAM_URL` (`wss://<same host>`, `ws://` on a local network) |
+| Adding a project fails | check the server's SSH key and its `known_hosts` |
+| Every run fails at once | Landlock isolation does not work on this kernel: read the run's error |
+| Starting answers 402 | monthly token budget reached: Administration → Quotas |
